# isEven and isOdd call each other in tail position, and main calls each
# where its result is still to be shown, so each returns to more than one
# place and neither becomes part of the other: each calls the other by a
# tail call. Each also recurses, so wherever it is inlined into main a call
# of it is left there, and the Bool it gives main is laid out as it returns
# it, in place, with nothing re-packed after the call.
owned: tail-calls=@Main.isEven:@Main.isOdd tail-calls=@Main.isOdd:@Main.isEven
owned: calls=@Main.main:@Main.isEven results-as-given=@Main.main:@Main.isEven
